/TEST 2 - FLAG DETECTION PART III / " C " LINES VERIFICATION PART III
/
/ (A)	THE SETTING OF THE MAINTENANCE FLIP-FLOP SHOULD "DIRECT SET" ALL
/	FLAGS (DONE, TRANSFER REQUEST, AND ERROR).
/
/ (B)	IF AN RX01 MICROCONTROLLER [IS] CABLED TO THE RX8 INTERFACE,
/	THEN THE SETTING OF THE MAINTENANCE FLIP-FLOP WILL ASSERT THE "RUN"
/	LINE (RESEMBLING A FILL BUFFER COMMAND) THUS CAUSING THE RX01
/	CONTROLLER TO SETUP FOR A "FILL BUFFER", BUT, HOWEVER, BECAUSE THE
/	MAINTENANCE FLIP-FLOP [IS] SET, THE RX8 INTERFACE RECEIVERS
/	SHOULD BE DISABLED AND NOT REACTIVE TO THE RX01 MICROCONTROLLER.
/
/WITH ALL FLAGS SET, THE RX8 INTERFACE IOT'S:
/
/ SDN - "SKIP ON DONE" (67X5), AND
/ SER - "SKIP ON ERROR" (67X4), AND,
/ STR - "SKIP ON TRANSFER REQUEST" (67X3) SHOULD SKIP
/
